#! /bin/sh

if [ -z "$2" ]; then
    printf 'Usage: !unclaude <url>\n'
    printf 'Example: !unclaude https://github.com/example/example-pr\n'
    exit 0
fi

printf 'Read the pull request description and author comments at ' "$1".

cat <<'EOT'
Understand the context and the intent, then write a short, clear summary of:
- what the change does or what the actual issue is;
- why the this is needed; and
- any important user-facing effect.

Use plain, common English and short sentences. Avoid jargon, unnecessary internal details, and overly verbose language.
EOT
